192
00:16:12,381 --> 00:16:17,846
Your assignment has four questions. One: the bight grows to 10 millimetres,

193
00:16:17,866 --> 00:16:21,283
with everything else as in the opening problem.

194
00:16:21,303 --> 00:16:24,940
For the modified-trapezoid and the cycloidal laws,

195
00:16:24,960 --> 00:16:30,498
find the inertia force at 5000 r/min and the highest speed that stays within

196
00:16:30,518 --> 00:16:31,229
the limit.

197
00:16:31,629 --> 00:16:34,440
Two: the hook radius is 13.5 millimetres.

198
00:16:34,460 --> 00:16:40,100
Find the catch difference between the two ends for bights of 6 and 10 millimetres.

199
00:16:40,120 --> 00:16:43,345
Using the loop window borrowed in this lecture,

200
00:16:43,365 --> 00:16:48,936
right end at the earliest about 198 degrees and left end at the latest about 218,

201
00:16:48,956 --> 00:16:52,871
decide whether 10 millimetres can be caught at both ends.

202
00:16:52,891 --> 00:16:57,220
Compare with the manual, and explain why it has to be measured.

203
00:16:57,620 --> 00:17:03,114
Three: an electronic bartacker moves its clamp 5 millimetres a step,

204
00:17:03,134 --> 00:17:06,682
over 170 degrees, with a modified trapezoid.

205
00:17:06,702 --> 00:17:10,979
Find the peak acceleration at 3200 stitches a minute.

206
00:17:10,999 --> 00:17:16,575
If the step grows to 8 millimetres with no more acceleration allowed,

207
00:17:16,595 --> 00:17:20,629
how far must the speed drop? Four, for discussion:

208
00:17:20,649 --> 00:17:25,981
an embroidery machine runs at about a quarter of lockstitch speed.

209
00:17:26,001 --> 00:17:30,360
Propose two ways to speed it up, and the cost of each.

210
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:32,388
Submit your working,

211
00:17:32,408 --> 00:17:37,663
the lab screenshots and the discussion on the WenQuest platform.

212
00:17:39,183 --> 00:17:47,232
There's also a ten-question quiz. For example, with an 8-millimetre bight,

213
00:17:47,252 --> 00:17:50,939
5000 r/min and a 170-degree swing,

214
00:17:50,959 --> 00:17:57,372
what is the peak acceleration under the modified trapezoid?

215
00:17:57,772 --> 00:18:03,139
Or, with everything else the same, the speed goes from 5000 to 6000.

216
00:18:03,159 --> 00:18:08,526
By what factor does the peak acceleration grow? And a true-or-false:

217
00:18:08,546 --> 00:18:13,992
the hook point sweeps right to left, so is the left end caught first?

218
00:18:14,392 --> 00:18:19,878
You get three attempts, and the explanations appear as soon as you submit.

219
00:18:21,398 --> 00:18:22,898
Three things to remember.

220
00:18:23,298 --> 00:18:27,192
One: every special machine obeys the same rule:

221
00:18:27,212 --> 00:18:33,604
no sideways relative motion between needle and fabric while the needle is in,

222
00:18:33,624 --> 00:18:38,933
so every sideways move is squeezed into the out-of-fabric angle.

223
00:18:39,333 --> 00:18:46,761
Two: peak acceleration is C times w times omega squared over beta squared,

224
00:18:46,781 --> 00:18:49,176
so use the whole window,

225
00:18:49,196 --> 00:18:54,913
and the modified trapezoid is both low-peaked and smooth.

226
00:18:55,313 --> 00:19:01,156
Three: the two ends of a zigzag are caught w over 2R apart,

227
00:19:01,176 --> 00:19:05,827
so the bight is limited by the catching window.

